      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "bug_description",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 18,
        "end_line": 49
      },
      "excerpt": "Description:\n\nThe issue reports that torch.div crashes with segmentation fault when using an incompatible out tensor shape.\n\nThe same behavior is also observed in torch.mul and torch.remainder.\n\n\nReproducer:\n\nimport torch\n\ntorch.div(\n    input=torch.ones([1]),\n    other=1,\n    out=torch.ones([5,1,1,1])\n)\n\n\ntorch.mul(\n    input=torch.ones([1]),\n    other=1,\n    out=torch.ones([5,1,1,1])\n)\n\n\ntorch.remainder(\n    input=torch.ones([1]),\n    other=1,\n    out=torch.ones([5,1,1,1])\n)\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": null,
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:825c7417f6accc350ec676cf20758491fa861205964b71515a0d42af26bf8051"
    },
    {
